m13 G160-V2.41: 2.41, 250, 1, 12.5, \"80 or 100\"\nm14 G250-V2.41: 2.41, 400, 2.5, 20, \"80 or 100\"\nm15 G250-V2.9: 2.9, 400, 2.5, 20, \"80 or 100 or 150\"\nm16 G400-V2.9: 2.9, 650, 4, 32, \"100 or 150\"\nm17 G250-V3.96: 3.96, 400, 2.5, 20, \"100 or 150\"\nm18 G400-V3.96: 3.96, 650, 4, 32, \"100 or 150\"\nm19 G650-V3.96: 3.96, 1000, 4, 32, \"150 or 200\"\nm20 G400-V6.34: 6.34, 650, 4, 32, \"150 or 200\"\nm21 G650-V6.34: 6.34, 1000, 6.5, 50, \"150 or 200\"\nm22 G650-V10.3: 10.3, 1000, 6.5, 50, \"150 or 200\"\nm23 G1000-V10.3: 10.3, 1600, 10, 80, \"150 or 200\"\n\nCheck m11 qmin: row \"2,32 G160 250 2,5 12,5\" — qmin 2.5, qt 12.5. Yes (unusual but as printed). m13: V2.41 G160: Qmax 250, Qmin 1, Qt 12.5. Yes.\n\nFootnote markers: cyclic_volume values get [\"*\"]; pmax config values get [\"**\"].\n\nMatrix table rows include footnote markers? rows are objects; I can't attach footnote_markers inside plain number values. I'll note in table footnotes array: [{marker: \"*\", applies_to: \"cyclic_volume\", text: ...}, {marker: \"**\", applies_to: \"maximum_pmax\", text: ...}].\n\nNow write JSON. Ensure numbers with dot decimals. Ensure no markdown fences. Output single JSON object.\n\nAlso include \"date_issued\"? absent — omit.\n\nissuing_authority: name \"NMi\". website? not present. Omit rest.\n\nLet me also decide whether to include accuracy_class in matrix rows: \"1.0 or 1.5\" string. Yes.\n\nWrite it out.",
